Package: FlowPredict
Title: Predictive Modelling of Groups and Immune Age from Cytometry Features
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      "Oliver", "Burton",
      email = "olivertburton@gmail.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre"),
      comment = c( ORCID = "0000-0003-3884-7373" )
    )
  )
Description:
    Answers two questions about a table of per-sample cytometry features
    (population frequencies, marker medians or any other numbers): which
    small set of features best separates two groups of samples, and how
    well; and how well the features predict a continuous variable such as
    age ("immune age").  Group prediction uses lasso logistic regression
    and random forests, evaluated by repeated, nested cross-validation, with
    feature importance and the smallest panel of features that reaches near
    the best performance.  The immune age model is an elastic net, evaluated
    the same way, with each sample's age gap corrected for regression to the
    mean and a permutation check against chance.  Folds can keep the samples
    of one donor together.  The design follows the nested cross-validation
    approach of Veiga et al. (2026, Nat Commun 17:4670), Humblet-Baron et al.
    (2025, Alzheimer's Dement 21:e70952) and Gemander et al. (2025, npj
    Vaccines 10:140), as implemented in the Honeychrome application.
